WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:09.406
Every date that matters in one place: live classes, asynchronous weeks, openings, deadlines, Study Week, and the end of term.

2
00:00:09.406 --> 00:00:20.352
Read the colours first. Seneca red marks due dates. Black marks live classes. Grey marks asynchronous weeks with no lecture, and a light outline marks Study Week.

3
00:00:20.352 --> 00:00:31.359
Scan the term at a glance. Deadlines follow the course rhythm: Compass Check in Week 7, Canadian Case File in Week 8, Design the Repair and the Map Exchange close in Week 12, then the final project on Sunday, December 13.

4
00:00:31.359 --> 00:00:42.364
Subscribe on your phone. The mobile calendar link is a live subscription, not a downloaded copy, so your calendar app can refresh when the course schedule changes.

5
00:00:42.364 --> 00:00:50.531
Treat Blackboard as the official source. If anything ever differs, Blackboard and your professor's announcements win.

6
00:00:50.531 --> 00:00:53.132
Nothing here is graded.

7
00:00:53.132 --> 00:00:59.242
Where next: Put the deadline weeks into your own planner now, before they are close.
